529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 262 0 R
/E (From January 2026 CBAM's transitional reporting requirements start tightening toward full certificate obligations. Indian exporters currently have no standardized way to produce the embedded-carbon documentation CBAM will require at the border. This system produces exactly that per-heat record, which is what turns a customs clearance from a manual, back-and-forth documentation request into a lookup.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
530 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 262 0 R
/E (Certifying a mill's carbon claims today means manual auditor visits and paper trails. An evidence-linked certificate \(Score-CAM images, SHAP attributions, hash-verifiable provenance\) gives a certifier something to check against rather than something to take on faith, cutting the manual verification burden per heat.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
